From: Carl Andersson <carl.andersson@dynamist.se>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-fs: show a read-only share's guest only an allowlist of paths

FsDevice::set_allowlist_file() names paths of a read-only share, one per
line, absolute below the share's root or relative to it. A directory
above a listed path shows only the names that lead to one, in a lookup
and in a listing; a listed path and everything below it are shared
unchanged. A host shares its whole Nix store this way and lists one
closure, with no bind mounts and so no mount namespace: the store view
vivarium builds on Linux does not exist on macOS.

When a lookup in a partial directory misses and the file has changed,
the device reads it again, so a host adds paths while the guest runs by
appending them.

PassthroughFsRo applies it, for every platform. A partial directory is
tracked by the inode its lookup returned and its path from the root;
InodeAllocator never reuses a number, so an entry stays valid after the
guest forgets the inode. readdirplus forgets the lookup it made for an
entry it hides.

The C header and the ffier schema are regenerated with ffier-gen-c-header
at the pinned v0.2.0-rc2; the header's only change is the new function.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5
